WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.862
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:07.680
SPEAKER 1: Under Compute
Engine in the Google

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:10.680
Cloud Platform console, go
to the VM Instances page

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:12.630
and click Create Instance.

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:14.670
Most of the field here
will be pre-populated

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:16.830
in order to speed up
the creation process,

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:19.395
but you're welcome to adjust
anything to suit your needs.

00:00:19.395 --> 00:00:21.270
For now, all you'll need
to do is add a name,

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:22.830
and in the Boot
Disk section click

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.470
Change to begin
configuring your boot disk.

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:27.570
The first tab is
the OS Images tab.

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:31.140
Here you should choose Debian
9 and then click Select.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:35.830
In the Firewall section
click Allow HTTP Traffic.

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:39.410
Click Create to
create your instance.

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:42.780
You can check the status
on the VM Instances page.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:44.910
Once ready, your instance
will be listed here

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:47.440
with a green status icon.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.390
After seeing that icon
next to your instance,

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:51.560
you're ready to connect.

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:53.420
To open a terminal
directly to the instance

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:56.100
you've just created,
click the SSH button.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.460
This will open a new
window and connect.

00:00:58.460 --> 00:00:59.450
Congratulations.

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:02.120
You now have a terminal window
for executing shell commands

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:05.247
and interacting directly
with your Linux instance.

00:01:05.247 --> 00:01:07.580
Make sure you delete any
instances you don't want to pay

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:09.710
for after this quick start.

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:12.460
[MUSIC PLAYING]

